  "question_stem": "{{figure:diagram_q01_01}}\n\nThe velocity of a particle moving in a straight line at time $t$ seconds after leaving a fixed point $O$ is $v \\text{ m s}^{-1}$. The diagram shows a velocity-time graph which models the motion of the particle from $t = 0$ to $t = T$. The graph consists of four straight line segments. The particle accelerates from rest to a speed of $V \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ over a period of $4 \\text{ s}$, and then decelerates at $\\frac{5}{3} \\text{ m s}^{-2}$ to instantaneous rest over a period of $6 \\text{ s}$. The particle then travels back towards $O$, reaching a maximum speed of $3 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ before coming to rest at time $t = T$.",
